  <decisions>[{"id": "PANEL-ITEM2-REJECT", "decision": "Item 2 as scoped (instrumentId = descriptors ‖ ladders ‖ classifier ‖ CLI_VERB_MAP ‖ corpus) is rejected unanimously; R-1 amended by its own author on 2 of 5 components", "rationale": "The classifier rule-set must not sit in a denominator-resetting id (rows are durable and scoring is pure, so a scorer fix should re-score, not re-run — and folding it in creates a standing incentive to leave the scorer broken). The corpus hash cannot be included because seed.ts:11-15 states no corpus exists. Jinx found seven further carriers the proposal still misses, including the primary metric itself, proving the enumeration SHAPE is wrong rather than its contents."}, {"id": "PANEL-ENFORCEMENT-FIRST", "decision": "Making summarizeBatch refuse a mixed-id or off-pin batch (~10 lines) proceeds without a founder decision", "rationale": "Unanimous across the panel and independent of every scope question. FG-3 is currently unenforced — verified: summarizeBatch never receives an id — so widening the freeze before enforcing it widens a field nobody reads."}, {"id": "PANEL-HOLD-FOR-PROBES", "decision": "Hold the item-2 shape decision and the sequencing decision pending two dispatched probes", "rationale": "Arky pre-registered Falsifier B against his own ruling and flagged it UNRUN and load-bearing: if a coverage test cannot go red on a new ladder while staying green on a comment edit, option (d) collapses into source-text hashing and the fallback is the far more expensive full relocation. North's B-2 reachability check may show F4 as ratified is unrunnable, which outranks every item in the queue. Both are ~20 minutes and both were pre-registered by the panel as preceding implementation."}]</decisions>
  <learnings>["FG-3 was never enforced: classifier.ts:266 collects descriptorsIds but summarizeBatch (completion.ts:159) never receives an id — two panels argued about the contents of a hash that no code path checks. Verify that a gate GATES before debating its scope.", "Hand-enumeration is the defect class, not the enumeration's contents. D-3 was a missed enumeration; the proposed fix enumerated again and was stale within 24 hours (it omitted src/f4/completion.ts, the primary metric, which landed a day later). The fix is a census that fails the build for any unregistered carrier — coverage by conjunction, not by memory.", "Source-text hashing is unimplementable in this package regardless of its merits: package.json declares files:['dist'] and tsup bundles every module into one chunk, so a runtime source hash is ENOENT when installed, different under npm link, different again in CI, and certifies a stale checkout under a bundled dist — the FG-3 defect class reintroduced one level up.", "Teaching change => re-run; instrument change => re-score. Rows are durable JSONL and classifyRun/evaluateCompletion are pure, so a scorer fix costs zero runs. Folding the scorer into the denominator-resetting id converts a free operation into an expensive one and creates a standing incentive to leave the scorer broken.", "Pre-registration protects PASSES, not FAILS. A kill-only screen cannot inflate a zero, so a freeze is a prerequisite for CLAIMING a pass and not for DISCOVERING a failure. Treating it as both is why the denominator has been zero for the entire arc.", "A panel's highest-value output is self-falsification, not consensus. Every one of the six panelists reported a finding against their own prior position, and those reversals — Arky amending R-1, Jinx reporting an attack as failed, Aegis withdrawing S4, Shield catching her own omission, North reversing twice, Loid finding his own framing uncomputable — carried more information than any agreement did.", "Mark provenance when recording panel findings into a permanent document: verified-by-Claude vs panel-asserted. source:external is not trust:external, and three of the panel's own citations to the PRIOR panel record had gone stale (D-2 closed, D-4 half-closed, D-5's line number drifted)."]</learnings>
